# 必考词 Unit10
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit10核心高频词汇

{{extent}}{/ɪkˈstent/}}{n. 程度；范围}}{{The extent of the damage is still being assessed.}}

{{external}}{/ɪkˈstɜːrnl/}}{adj. 外部的；外面的}}{{The building suffered external damage from the storm.}}

{{extraordinary}}{/ɪkˈstrɔːrdnri/}}{adj. 非凡的；特别的}}{{She has extraordinary talent in music.}}

{{extreme}}{/ɪkˈstriːm/}}{adj. 极端的；n. 极端}}{{Extreme weather events have become more frequent.}}

{{fabric}}{/ˈfæbrɪk/}}{n. 织物；结构}}{{The fabric of society is built on trust and cooperation.}}

{{facilitate}}{/fəˈsɪlɪteɪt/}}{v. 促进；使便利}}{{Technology facilitates communication across distances.}}

{{factor}}{/ˈfæktər/}}{n. 因素；要素}}{{Cost is an important factor in the decision-making process.}}

{{faculty}}{/ˈfækəlti/}}{n. 全体教员；能力}}{{The faculty of the university is highly qualified.}}

{{fade}}{/feɪd/}}{v. 褪色；消退}}{{The memory of the event gradually faded with time.}}

{{failure}}{/ˈfeɪljər/}}{n. 失败；故障}}{{Failure is the mother of success.}}

{{faith}}{/feɪθ/}}{n. 信仰；信任}}{{She has great faith in her children's abilities.}}

{{fame}}{/feɪm/}}{n. 名声；声誉}}{{The actor rose to fame after his first film.}}

{{fancy}}{/ˈfænsi/}}{adj. 精致的；v. 想象；喜欢}}{{She wore a fancy dress to the party.}}

{{fatal}}{/ˈfeɪtl/}}{adj. 致命的；毁灭性的}}{{The accident was fatal to three passengers.}}

{{favor}}{/ˈfeɪvər/}}{n. 恩惠；赞同；v. 偏爱}}{{Can you do me a favor and pick up my mail?}}

{{feasible}}{/ˈfiːzəbl/}}{adj. 可行的；可能的}}{{The plan is technically feasible but expensive.}}

{{feature}}{/ˈfiːtʃər/}}{n. 特征；特色}}{{The phone has many advanced features.}}

{{federal}}{/ˈfedərəl/}}{adj. 联邦的}}{{The federal government announced new tax policies.}}

{{figure}}{/ˈfɪɡər/}}{n. 数字；人物；身材}}{{The figure shows a significant increase in sales.}}

{{finance}}{/ˈfaɪnæns/}}{n. 金融；v. 提供资金}}{{She studied finance at a business school.}}

{{fierce}}{/fɪərs/}}{adj. 猛烈的；凶猛的}}{{The competition for the scholarship is fierce.}}

{{file}}{/faɪl/}}{n. 文件；v. 提交；锉}}{{Please submit the file before the deadline.}}

{{fine}}{/faɪn/}}{adj. 好的；罚款；n. 罚金}}{{He was fined for parking illegally.}}

{{firm}}{/fɜːrm/}}{adj. 坚定的；n. 公司}}{{She is firm in her belief that education changes lives.}}

{{fiscal}}{/ˈfɪskl/}}{adj. 财政的；国库的}}{{The government introduced new fiscal policies to stimulate growth.}}

{{fix}}{/fɪks/}}{v. 修理；固定；确定}}{{The mechanic fixed the engine in less than an hour.}}

{{flaw}}{/flɔː/}}{n. 缺陷；瑕疵}}{{The plan has a serious flaw that needs to be addressed.}}

{{flee}}{/fliː/}}{v. 逃走；逃避}}{{Thousands of refugees fled the war-torn country.}}

{{flexible}}{/ˈfleksəbl/}}{adj. 灵活的；可变通的}}{{The company offers flexible working hours to its employees.}}

{{float}}{/fləʊt/}}{v. 漂浮；飘动}}{{The boat floated gently on the calm lake.}}

{{flourish}}{/ˈflʌrɪʃ/}}{v. 繁荣；茂盛}}{{The arts flourished during the Renaissance period.}}

{{flow}}{/fləʊ/}}{v./n. 流动；流量}}{{The river flows through the heart of the city.}}

{{fluctuate}}{/ˈflʌktʃueɪt/}}{v. 波动；涨落}}{{Oil prices have fluctuated dramatically this year.}}

{{focus}}{/ˈfəʊkəs/}}{v./n. 集中；焦点}}{{We need to focus on the most important tasks first.}}

{{forbid}}{/fəˈbɪd/}}{v. 禁止；不许}}{{Smoking is forbidden in all public buildings.}}

{{forecast}}{/ˈfɔːrkɑːst/}}{v./n. 预测；预报}}{{The weather forecast predicts heavy rain tomorrow.}}

{{former}}{/ˈfɔːrmər/}}{adj. 以前的；前任的}}{{The former president gave a speech at the ceremony.}}

{{formula}}{/ˈfɔːrmjələ/}}{n. 公式；方案}}{{The scientist developed a new formula for the chemical compound.}}

{{fortune}}{/ˈfɔːrtʃuːn/}}{n. 命运；财富}}{{He made his fortune in the technology industry.}}

{{fossil}}{/ˈfɒsl/}}{n. 化石}}{{The fossils found in the area date back millions of years.}}
